                    },
                    "message": "@vvlprabha@gmail.com I see all the versions in this file at chassis level. Probably the non-chassis level are coming from the new updaters. Can you share the example of non-chassis level you are referring to?\nIf what i said above is true we need to make sure the new versions are same what was being reported through settingsd. What you done that?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prabha Veerubhotla",
                        "email": "vvlprabha@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Prabha-Veerubhotla"
                    },
                    "message": "yes verified that the new and old versions are same for\n1. Harma_MB_mb_cpld \n2. Harma_MB_retimer0 \n3. Harma_MB_retimer1 \n4. Harma_SCM_scm_cpld \n\nfor \n1. Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_pvdd11 \n2. Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_vcore0 \n3. Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_vcore1 \n\nthe old versions are in decimal format and new version is in hexadecimal format."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> yes verified that the new and old versions are same for\n> 1. Harma_MB_mb_cpld \n> 2. Harma_MB_retimer0 \n> 3. Harma_MB_retimer1 \n> 4. Harma_SCM_scm_cpld \n> \n> for \n> 1. Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_pvdd11 \n> 2. Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_vcore0 \n> 3. Harma_MB_vr_cpu0_vcore1 \n> \n> the old versions are in decimal format and new version is in hexadecimal format.\n\nThe old version was in hex and new VR updater prints it in decimal for VR. https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/82119 should bring in change by Kevin (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/82054) which will fix this."
                }
